    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math> are two complex numbers such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>arg</mi><mfenced><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>arg</mi><mfenced><mi>&#969;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>arg</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math> is:<br />(Here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>arg</mi><mfenced><mi>z</mi></mfenced></math> denotes the principal argument of complex number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>)",
